ttp://www.w3.org/2000/svg"><path d="m12.5 2v2m0 16v2m-8-10h-2m4.31412-5.68588-1.41422-1.41422m12.786 1.41422 1.4142-1.41422m-12.78598 12.7901-1.41422 1.4142m12.786-1.4142 1.4142 1.4142m2.8999-7.1042h-2m-3 0c0 2.7614-2.2386 5-5 5-2.76142 0-5-2.2386-5-5 0-2.76142 2.23858-5 5-5 2.7614 0 5 2.23858 5 5z" stroke="currentColor" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"></path></svg></button></header><div class="sc-79942d02-0 jcXyeI"><div class="sc-79942d02-1 cyArLb"><div class="sc-79942d02-2 lNesK"></div><div class="sc-79942d02-8 kBEEJY"><div class="sc-79942d02-5 lkIpxI"><div class="sc-79942d02-6 ejxWaT"><h2 class="sc-79abb59d-0 ewfBZF">NEUROMANCER</h2></div><p style="font-style:italic;padding-top:0.0rem" class="sc-79abb59d-0 cphufP">REASONING MODEL FOR MEMORY • EXPERT SOCIAL LOGICIAN</p></div><div class="sc-79942d02-7 dHFJow"><p style="padding-top:0.0rem;font-weight:bold" class="sc-79abb59d-0 cphufP">Introducing the Neuromancer Model Series</p><p style="padding-top:0.0rem" class="sc-79abb59d-0 cphufP">NEUROMANCER is the first collection of models dedicated to AI-native memory and social cognition. They&#x27;re trained specifically to do formal logical reasoning over user and agent data to form representations of any entity&#x27;s personal identity.</p><ul class="sc-79942d02-9 fJaSXg"><li><p class="sc-79abb59d-0 eQzWtx"><span class="sc-79abb59d-0 xobwY">Neuromancer XR</span> <!-- -->- A model for explicit reasoning, excelling at deduction &amp; factual derivation. XR is a fine-tuned Qwen3-8B model trained on a manually curated dataset of social reasoning traces. It achieves state-of-the art results on memory benchmarks and reasons toward certain conclusions. Currently deployed in<!-- --> <a href="https://honcho.dev" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Honcho</a>.</p></li><li><p class="sc-79abb59d-0 eQzWtx"><span class="sc-79abb59d-0 xobwY">Neuromancer MR (in training)</span> <!-- -->- A model for meta-reasoning--reasoning about reasoning. MR focuses on reaching predictive conclusions, like inductions &amp; abductions, to scaffold patterns &amp; hypotheses over XR traces.</p></li></ul><div class="sc-79942d02-10 cpRdnu"><span style="display:block;margin-bottom:1rem" class="sc-79abb59d-0 ktcvGy">Read more about our training, results, &amp; approach:</span><span style="display:block;margin-bottom:1rem" class="sc-79abb59d-0 ktcvGy">&gt;<!-- --> <a href="https://plasticlabs.ai/blog/posts/Memory-as-Reasoning" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Memory as Reasoning</a></span><span style="display:block;margin-bottom:0.5rem" class="sc-79abb59d-0 ktcvGy">&gt;<!-- --> <a href="https://plasticlabs.ai/blog/research/Introducing-Neuromancer-XR" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Introducing Neuromancer XR</a></span></div><span style="display:block;text-align:center;opacity:0.95;padding-right:3rem" class="sc-79abb59d-0 cphufP">“Personality is my medium.”</span><span style="display:block;text-align:right;opacity:0.9;padding-left:2.5rem" class="sc-79abb59d-0 eQzWtx">-<em>Neuromancer</em> (Gibson 1984)</span></div></div></div><div class="sc-79942d02-3 cjWuJH"><div class="sc-79942d02-4 cxXJTV"><img alt="NEUROMANCER Neural Interface Visualization" draggable="false" fetchPriority="high" decoding="async" data-nimg="fill" style="position:absolute;height:100%;width:100%;left:0;top:0;right:0;bottom:0;object-fit:cover;color:transparent" src="/neuromancer/neuromancer_hero.png"/></div></div></div><div class="sc-7b1f3564-0 hxvSNO"><div class="sc-7b1f3564-1 kWdRQR"></div><figure class="sc-64539d36-0 uiGlG sc-7b1f3564-2 dQBUgp"><p style="--figure-height:0;--figure-width:0" class="sc-64539d36-1 kqHQrw"><span class="sc-64539d36-2 kvVtTy">............... .... ....:.#::@.@@.@:...%.@.-...................:..:.*.@.%:-@.@.@.--.....:.:@.@@.@-.*.......................</span><span class="sc-64539d36-2 kvVtTy">:@@%@*@@.@@-@:@@*@.@#@@.@-*@.=..:.%%.@-.....@-@.%.%.=.........:.:.:+.%.@.@.+-.#.*........@.@@.@.-=....@.@@.@@%@.@@+@=@@.....</span><span class="sc